+**Head-class governance: `prefill-interleave: head`.** Instead of a counted hold, each step is
+governed by the class of the oldest active request: while that request is prefilling its prompt,
+the decode lanes are frozen (no decode rows in the step); while it is decoding, prefill and
+admission are frozen (no chunk, no new request enters). The policy self-ages -- the governing
+request always moves toward finishing, and a preempted request keeps its arrival, so its recompute
+governs as a prefill from the queue -- and carries no starvation timer and no hysteresis. KNOWN
+TRADE: a new prompt's time to first token has a floor of the summed remaining decode of every
+older request, and frozen decoders keep their KV (they are never preempted while frozen), so the
+pool is not freed for the prefill until a flip or `preempt-wait-ms` pressure reclaims it. Expert
+staging disarms on every flip (`head_flips`: on an expert-tiered box each flip re-stages the
+resident set). `/stats` counts the frozen-lane steps as `steps_held_decode`, the flips as
+`head_flips`, and the liveness passes that lifted a freeze because the step would otherwise have
+idled as `head_freeze_releases` (each occurrence is a near-stall; watch it at ~0). A step issued
+ahead keeps its overlap under decode-govern. `prefill-interleave: auto/N` stays the safe default.
+
 **A prefill alone in its step can carry several intervals** (`prefill-span: N`, default 1). A
 chunk ends on every checkpoint interval, so a prompt is otherwise prefilled one interval a step.
 With
